fire  and blood  hey guys pete here i was not expecting a  teaser for house of the dragon to come  out in the middle of the afternoon my  time when literally nothing has ever  come out before but it's here and this  looks pretty amazing this idea always  gets thrown out there whether people  care about game of thrones anymore or  not for as popular as it was and as  generally unpopular as the final season  turned out to be it always comes up  whether people will have a desire to  revisit westeros or not myself i'm still  anxiously anticipating the next book the  winds of winter i'll read that as soon  as it comes out but i kind of got burned  out with the waiting and hadn't really  been drawn to anything short of its  release until recently shooting has been  underway for a while on house of the  dragon and there have been a lot of  leaked set photos popping up and i do  find myself getting sucked into looking  at those it was always so much fun to  look at those when game of thrones was  filming and try to speculate on what was  coming next and while it isn't quite the  same old habits do die hard and when you  add a teaser on top of that i find  myself completely paying attention again  before i get into the teaser i'll give  you a really quick overview of what to  expect from house of the dragon it's  taken from the fictional history of the  targaryen family called fire and blood  by george rr martin the show will be  focusing on the civil war of succession  known as the dance of the dragons that  happened after king becerrus the first  died he had named his only surviving  daughter from his first marriage renera  as his successor before remarrying and  having more children with alison  hightower after his death both sides  known as the greens and the blacks could  make a credible claim to put their  favored successor on the iron throne  different factions back them for  political reasons and things escalated  until war broke out it's called the  dance of the dragons because this all  happened 200 years before the events of  game of thrones when the family still  had a lot of living dragons the other  name given to this period is the death  of the dragons because by the end of it  there are a lot of casualties  as i mentioned the trailer looks  fantastic we get a look at the major  players on both sides some valyrian  steel blades and we get our first look  at the valerians which is another family  with the blood of old valyria who didn't  play a huge role during the game of  thrones timeline one of the first things  that pops out is this new imagining of  the iron throne it still looks like the  same one they used in game of thrones  but they added to it to make it look  more like it was imagined in the books i  guess they can say that later on it was  changed and that's how you get the  consistency between the two shows it's  missing any live action scenes with  dragons but there is this one shot where  it's probably the skull of valerian the  black dread we see renera at different  ages in her life when she was younger  when her father was still alive and she  was known as the realms delight they  cast two different actors emma darcy and  millie alcock to play the role so it's  been known that there would be multiple  timelines involved both appear in the  teaser depicting the character at  different ages during the dance she was  married to her uncle damon targaryen  played by matt smith who is in several  scenes in this trailer including this  really nice looking torny shot where it  looks like he's fighting kristin cole  the targaryen armor here looks fantastic  and you get a pretty good look at his  valyrian steel blade dark sister which  has wings and a dragon egg pommel you  even catch a quick glimpse of a stark  banner in a different tourney scene  which is a nice touch and based on their  shields the jousters here look like  they're from house tarly for sure and  then maybe house coal if you were  wondering i mentioned that we get our  first looks at house valerian we see  corliss who is known as the sea snake  he's an important character with a great  backstory and a group shot where it  looks like they're approaching the  wedding where rhaenyra and lane or  valerian will be married on the green  side of things we see a glimpse of otto  hightower as the hand of the king he  served under viserys and then later we  see his daughter allison running with a  dagger in her hand and it looks like  it's that same cat spa dagger that  showed up in the final season of game of  thrones so it looks like it plays an  important role in both series i'm  guessing that this comes after one of  her sons loses his eye but there's not a  lot to go off of right here there's a  quick shot of king becerris on the  throne holding blackfyre and a shot of  mazaria who's connected to daemon and  even serves as his mistress of whispers  at one point there's a fight inside what  looks like one of house valerian's  castles and so yeah there's a little bit  of everything and just one more time it  looks great and it's really sparked my  interest the costumes are up to the  level you'd hope for and at least in  this edited footage the wigs don't look  that bad to me although they're not the  first thing i noticed so maybe i'm not  the best judge there's no release date  yet but we know it won't be coming out  until next year  no major revelations in what they show  it's still unclear how the timelines are  going to work and exactly how much time  they'll be covering in this first season  the iron throne catspaw dagger house  sigils and valyrian steel blades that  feeling is coming back and i'm excited  to hear what people have to say about  this i think that's a good place to  leave it but let me know what you think  in the comments and what you're hoping  to see please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon

